  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 152 AM CDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nUpper level high pressure remains anchored to the north of the \narea across the southern United States. The main change is that\nmid and lower level flow becomes more southerly, advecting in\nwarmer temperatures from Mexico and causing temps to increase a\nfew degrees. This could bring a brief return of 100 degree highs\nlate in the week. There is model disagreement over the weekend\nwith regards to a cold front moving into the South Plains. Poor\nmodel to model and run to run consistency leaves great uncertainty\nas to whether the front (and it's cooling effects) will make it \ninto our CWA. The NBM is showing slight cooling early next week\nwith an increase in rain chances. \n\nHennig",
